      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T17:31:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like a good change. Is there a reason to restrict it to just Dewatt, versus making it the default behavior for all boards?\n\nLooking around a bit, the common function was created with: [lid_angle: Create a common callback for lid angle changes](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3069175)\n\nThat CL shows a lot of boards are using the implementation you\u0027re adding here, so moving this up to `src/platform/ec/common/lid_angle.c` would clean up a lot of duplication. I don\u0027t see any discussion about that in the linked CL, so it doesn\u0027t seem it was explicitly not included as part of that cleanup for any reason.",
      "revId": "7f00fc620e6848524550790861611175ca75fc3d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b13040e_fff0aafa",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T17:50:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It isn\u0027t the default because of the reason in that comment I linked, which led to b/159456704 for Zork.\nTo make it default, we would need to decide to no longer support the feature that the OS offers of \"external display is primary and tablet mode device is keyboard + trackpad\".\nIt is a pretty obscure feature, and presumably broken on quite a few boards, and not caught in testing.",
      "parentUuid": "b557fe16_a8de88c8",
      "revId": "7f00fc620e6848524550790861611175ca75fc3d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c4ca61d_4c6854a6",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1297197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T18:01:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Then they\u0027re probably broken. :) If you have one of those devices, you can connect an external display, lower the brightness of the internal panel until the external display becomes the primary, put the device in tablet mode and verify that the internal keyboard and trackpad still work.\n\nSo a device in tablet mode with an external display attached should still allow the keyboard to work(?). And we get into tablet mode, because the internal display was disabled(?).\n\nThat seems unexpected to me. Specifically, why does disabling the internal display enable tablet mode? The S0 check feels more like a workaround for that unexpected behavior than a fix for a well-defined state.",
      "parentUuid": "1b13040e_fff0aafa",
      "revId": "7f00fc620e6848524550790861611175ca75fc3d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66089648_977e3a17",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T18:23:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree it is unexpected, but it was a deliberate feature not a workaround.\nHere is another bug about it: b/252374628 -\u003e b/181370314 -\u003e \"This is a user visible feature that has been broken for over 1.5 years now\".\n\n\u003e why does disabling the internal display enable tablet mode?\n\nIt doesn\u0027t. You disable the internal display to make the external the primary. Then you put the device physically in tablet mode and place it screen down to use the keyboard with the external display.",
      "parentUuid": "1c4ca61d_4c6854a6",
      "revId": "7f00fc620e6848524550790861611175ca75fc3d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "529730cf_377e539f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1297197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T21:07:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on that, we:\n\n1. Should not land this CL, since it will regress behavior.\n2. Should remove every other instance where this code is implemented.\n3. Add a test to formalize the expected behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "66089648_977e3a17",
      "revId": "7f00fc620e6848524550790861611175ca75fc3d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
